{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-10T13:46:56.247Z","data":{"text":"All done. Summary of what was executed:\n\n**Task 2 of change 166** — showing a recorded after-land failure in the inbox, `osq status`, and the dashboard:\n\n- **`src/core/status/inbox.ts`** — `NeedsYouKind` gained `after-land-failed`; the union declaration is written on one line under a `biome-ignore format` comment (the same pattern `state.ts` uses) so the file stays within the 250-line source budget (245 lines).\n- **`src/core/status/inbox-projection.ts`** — `readInbox` reads the record through task 1's `readAfterLandFailure(projectRoot, options.home)` and adds exactly `{ kind: 'after-land-failed', change: { id, title }, task: null, command: 'osq land <id>' }`, title from `parseSpecMdFromFolder` on the archived folder in the checkout's archive directory or else the folder name, sorted with the other items.\n- **`src/core/status/inbox-text.ts`** — renders `  <id>: <title> — after-land command failed — osq land <id>`.\n- **`src/cli/status.ts`** — `statusCommand` prints `After-land command failed for <id>: <command> — osq land <id>` after the watcher and log lines when a record exists.\n- **`packages/ui/src/home/labels.ts`** — `NEEDS_YOU_LABELS` gained `after-land-failed: 'after-land failed'`.\n- **`tests/inbox-after-land.test.ts`** (new) — covers both scenarios of \"Failed after-land command in status and inbox\" through `readInbox`, `formatInboxText`, and `statusCommand`, and \"After-land failed label\" through `needsYouKindLabel`, plus a round-trip through task 1's `readAfterLandFailure`.\n\nBoth verifies pass: the task's `node --import tsx ... --test tests/inbox-after-land.test.ts` (3/3) and the proposal's `pnpm verify` (typecheck, build, full test suite, lint all green). Result written to `.run/results/2.md`."}}
